---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import CardGroup from '../components/CardGroup.astro';
import RouteCard from '../components/RouteCard.astro';
import StepList from '../components/StepList.astro';
import Step from '../components/Step.astro';

// Copy: rewritten from content-source/waypoint-content-v1.md, section "9 How referrals work".
// Wes's build notes: separate a first enquiry from an agreed offer and confirmed start. No live
// referral form, upload or download; detailed records go through a secure route agreed later.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How alternative provision referrals work"
  description="How referrals to Waypoint work, from a first question to an agreed placement, for schools, local authorities and home-educating families."
>
  <PageHero
    title="How alternative provision referrals work"
    strapline="From a first enquiry to an agreed placement, step by step."
  />

  <Section
    id="referrals"
    title="Referrals"
    strapline="It all starts with a question."
    drawing="signpost"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of a stick person looking up at a signpost"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You don't need a completed referral pack to get in touch. There are two routes, depending on whether a school
          is arranging the place or your family home educates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <CardGroup columns={2}>
      <RouteCard title="School-funded places" href="#school-funded-places">
        Your headteacher or senior team looks at Waypoint as a provider first. Then your SENCo or inclusion lead talks
        to us about the pupil.
      </RouteCard>
      <RouteCard title="Home education" href="#home-education">
        Home-educating families can ask us directly, with no referral or school approval needed.
      </RouteCard>
    </CardGroup>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="school-funded-places"
    title="School-funded places"
    strapline="Six steps, from first question to review."
    drawing="meeting"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of two adults and a young person talking round a table"
    drawingSide="left"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Nothing is confirmed until it's been agreed in writing, and an enquiry or a referral doesn't guarantee a
          place.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <div class="steps">
      <StepList>
        <Step title="First enquiry" who="A school, local authority or parent">
          <p>
            Ask us about Waypoint and what a place could be for. Keep the first message general and don't send any
            details that identify a young person. We'll explain the next step.
          </p>
        </Step>
        <Step title="Talking about suitability" who="Wes, with the school">
          <p>
            We look at the young person's strengths, interests, support needs and any risks, and what the placement
            should achieve, alongside the group, setting and staff available.
          </p>
        </Step>
        <Step title="Sharing information" who="The school, through an agreed secure route">
          <p>
            We use the documents you already have rather than asking you to rewrite them. Depending on the young person,
            we may need the following.
          </p>
          <ul class="info-list">
            <li>The reason for the referral and what it should achieve</li>
            <li>Relevant education, support and risk plans</li>
            <li>Communication, sensory and emotional support information</li>
            <li>Medical needs, allergies and medication arrangements</li>
            <li>The young person's views and what helps them</li>
            <li>Family, school and emergency contacts</li>
            <li>Arrival, collection and transport arrangements</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We'll say exactly what's needed and point out any gaps that affect suitability or safety.</p>
        </Step>
        <Step title="Agreeing the offer" who="Waypoint and the school">
          <p>
            If the place is suitable and available, we agree dates, goals, support, communication, reviews, fees and
            funding. The school also authorises the placement and funding, and finance and purchasing are agreed before a
            start date is confirmed.
          </p>
        </Step>
        <Step title="Getting ready to start" who="Waypoint">
          <p>
            We normally need five working days once we have complete information, and an earlier start is sometimes
            possible. We confirm the start date directly. Before the first day we talk about the young person's
            interests and the support that helps, agree arrival, handover and collection, and arrange any visit in
            advance.
          </p>
        </Step>
        <Step title="Reviews" who="Waypoint, with the school and family">
          <p>
            We review how the young person is taking part, their goals, the support and their own experience. If their
            needs or circumstances change, we review sooner.
          </p>
        </Step>
      </StepList>
    </div>
    <div class="button-row">
      <Button href="/contact/?purpose=placement">Discuss a pupil</Button>
      <Button href="/for-schools/#arranging-a-placement" variant="secondary">More for schools</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="home-education"
    title="Home education"
    strapline="Just ask us directly."
    drawing="campfire"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of stick people sitting and standing round a campfire"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          If you home educate, you don't need a referral. Tell us about the projects your child might enjoy and what
          you're looking for. We'll talk through the group, the proposed fees, availability and arrangements before
          anything is booked. The school-funded steps above don't automatically apply.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <Button href="/contact/?purpose=home-education">Ask about home education</Button>
        <Button href="/home-education/" variant="secondary">Home education at Waypoint</Button>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="parents"
    title="Parents and carers"
    strapline="If your child is at school."
    drawing="helping"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of an adult showing a young person how to stack blocks"
    drawingSide="left"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You're always welcome to ask us a general question. To explore a school-funded place, your child's SENCo or
          inclusion lead takes it forward once the school is happy with Waypoint as a provider and the funding is
          agreed.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="more-link"><a href="/parents-and-carers/">Information for parents and carers</a></p>
    </Fragment>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="ask-a-question"
    title="Ask a question"
    strapline="No referral pack needed."
    brand
    drawing="chat"
    drawingLabel="Line drawing of two stick people chatting, with speech bubbles"
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Asking a question isn't a referral or a booking. Keep your first message general, and we'll explain the next
          step.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <Button href="/contact/" variant="accent">Ask a question</Button>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .steps {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .info-list {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .info-list li + li {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .more-link {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .more-link a::after {
    content: ' \2192';
  }
</style>
